node_modules/
.env

# Build output. Not tracked.
#
# It was tracked, so that main could be served straight from a checkout. What
# that cost: every commit made from a stale or partial checkout silently
# rewrote it, and the resulting diff — one line, a hashed filename changing —
# reads as routine. `ed4bf1a` looked exactly like that and was a complete
# revert of the commit before it.
#
# To be clear about what this does and does not fix: that commit removed source
# files too, and ignoring dist/ would not have stopped it. Pulling before
# committing is what stops that. This only removes the misleading signal.
#
# The consequence, which is real: main is no longer servable as-is. Whoever
# serves it runs `npm run build` first, with the environment variables set.
#
# They have to be set at build time, not run time: Vite inlines
# import.meta.env.VITE_* into the bundle, so a build made without them produces
# an app that throws on boot. VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY belongs in client
# JavaScript — that is what an anon key is for, and RLS is what guards the data.
# The service role key must never reach a build.
dist/

.superpowers/
images/

# Vite writes these beside the config when it has to transpile it — one per
# run, named with a timestamp. Build artefacts of the build tool itself, and
# they appear on any machine that runs the dev server.
vite.config.ts.timestamp-*
